    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0603" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg597"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Newport, R. I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 10th instant stating that the Department has signified to
                    the chargé d’affaires <hi rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of Germany its
                    cordial concurrence in the appointment of Mr. Schmidt, late vice-consul of
                    Germany at Apia, as president of the municipal council in Samoa.</p>
                <p>I have informed Lord Rosebery by telegram of the fact, as well as of the
                    acceptance by Mr. Ide of the post of chief justice of Samoa, which you were good
                    enough to communicate to me in your note of the 6th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
